Canonical residue-transversals mod (2n-1): for each pair a in 1..n-1 pick
choice in {a (lower), 2n-1-a (upper)}. Flip-set F = pairs choosing upper.
AP = F empty. Tabulate M(T) by |F| and list the FLOOR (M=1/n) flip-sets.
========================================================================

 n=5 (2n-1=9, floor=1/5, edge=2/9):
   FLOOR transversals (M=1/n): 2
      F=()  S=(1, 2, 3, 4)
      F=(2,)  S=(1, 3, 4, 7)
   min M among NON-floor transversals = 3/13  (edge=2/9=0.2222); >= edge? True
   min M by flip-count |F|:
      |F|=0: 1 sets, min M=1/5
      |F|=1: 4 sets, min M=1/5
      |F|=2: 5 sets, min M=3/13
      |F|=3: 4 sets, min M=1/4
      |F|=4: 1 sets, min M=5/13

